// AzureService covers all Azure-side observability operations: enabling
// the global logs.analytics block in azure.yaml, listing services, running
// historical KQL queries, polling/streaming Azure logs, performing setup
// + diagnostics checks, listing Log Analytics tables, and persisting the
// per-service log configuration (tables vs custom KQL).
//
// Every RPC below cites the legacy Go function and source file it
// preserves byte-for-byte. The point of this rewrite (PR 1, commit A
// of the Azure migration) is to lock the wire shape to what the
// dashboard already consumes today via REST, so the parallel Connect
// surface can replace REST one consumer at a time without dashboard
// drift. New behavior does NOT belong in this commit; aspirational
// fields were stripped.
//
// Two responses still pass through google.protobuf.Struct
// (GetAzureSetupState and GetAzureDiagnostics). Both are tracked in the
// ADR's "Struct Usage Inventory" subsection; the rationale lives there.

